course: dictionary
lesson: 16180
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yana is not an ordinary English word, so you cannot work out its meaning from the usual clues alone. Context helps you decide which meaning fits. «Yana sat next to me at lunch.» Here Yana is a person, so it is a girl's name, said "YAH-nuh".
explain: Some names come from other countries and are written in other alphabets. Yana is common in Ukraine, Russia, Bulgaria and other countries. In Ukrainian it is written Яна, so the sound is a good clue when the spelling looks strange.
explain: In Buddhism lessons, yana comes from Sanskrit and means "vehicle" or "path". You may see it inside longer words, such as Mahayana and Vajrayana. Yana can also be the name of a river in Siberia, so always ask which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Yana is a girl's name, said "YAH-nuh".
fact: Yana is common in Ukraine, Russia, Bulgaria and other countries.
fact: In Ukrainian, Yana is written Яна.
fact: In Sanskrit, "yana" means "vehicle" or "path".
fact: Yana is also the name of a river in Siberia, Russia.
exercise: «Yana kicked the ball back to her team.» What is Yana in this sentence? | *A girl's name | A vehicle | A river in Siberia | A kind of food
exercise: In Sanskrit, what does "yana" mean? | Golden light | Ocean | Snow or ice | *Vehicle or path
exercise: Which longer word from Buddhism contains yana? | Bulgaria | Sanskrit | Siberia | *Mahayana
test: Besides Ukraine and Bulgaria, which country is Yana common in? | Egypt | Brazil | *Russia | Japan
test: Which spelling shows Yana in Ukrainian? | Siberia | Mahayana | Vajrayana | *Яна
exam: A book says: «Mahayana means great vehicle.» What does yana mean inside Mahayana? | A river | *Vehicle or path | A country | A girl's name
